Issue 02 done, committed as 81a74ba (engine paths only; `.scratch/` left to the runner).

**What landed:**
- Three interrupt kinds in `engine/engine.ts`: `checkpoint` (body = the Issue's `## Brief`), `crash` (body = log path; detected by an `in-progress` marker read-back), `deadlock` (body = blockers that can never complete, via `canComplete` over the blocked-by closure covering cycles, unknown blocker ids, and deadlock propagation)
- Interrupts pause only their own subtree; siblings keep running in later super-steps
- `PoolRun.resume(ticketId, note?)` appends a `## Resume note` to the Issue, reloads markers from disk, restarts the ticket, and continues the pool in one action; resumes are serialized and a disk-side `status=done` fix is respected
- Phase vocabulary: `quiescent` (interrupts pending) vs `done` vs the residual `stalled`
- 13 new/rewritten seam tests, 106 total passing, `tsc --noEmit` clean; two-axis review ran and its should-fixes (store leak on throw, assignment re-resolution, resume serialization) are in the commit

Issue file set to `status=done` with review findings recorded for Issues 03+.
